 ## Subtopics
+
+### [Simple Reflections](1234-simple-reflections.md)
+Simple Reflections is a local illumination technique that approximates specular highlights by raymarching along the geometric reflection vector at a surface hit point and blending the resulting color with the base surface color. It is chosen when iterative numerical evaluation is acceptable and memory for precomputed spectra is constrained. Unlike this method, which uses polynomial expansion for analytical evaluation, Simple Reflections relies on iterative numerical raymarching. [Simple Reflections](1234-simple-reflections.md)
 
